# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the Duet2 Maestro printer config on
# the SAM4S backend. Boots klipper firmware under Renode against the
# duet2-maestro pin map, completes klippy identify + clocksync, reads
# thermistors through adc_scaled (vref_scaled), and walks DUMP_TMC /
# SET_TMC_FIELD against the renode software-UART hook
# (renode_hooks.sw_uart). Exercises the full chain of changes this
# config requires that smoke tests don't:
#
#   - sw_uart driving PA9 RX from CPU PC hooks on tmcuart_read_event
#     (firmware uses separate uart_pin/tx_pin, not single-wire AVR)
#   - test/emulator/sam4s_adc_stub.py replacing Renode's read-only
#     Analog.SAM4S_ADC (vref/vssa per-channel overrides land so
#     adc_scaled doesn't divide by zero)
#   - local sam4s8c.repl pinning DWT.frequency to CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ
#   - control-socket early-bind in renode_launcher so the fixture
#     pusher hits a listening socket while Renode is still booting
#
# G28 / G1 / SET_HEATER_TEMP are intentionally OMITTED: Renode's JIT
# CPU executes the firmware at a wall-clock-bound rate that drifts
# from the configured 120 MHz CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ (klippy logs "MCU
# 'mcu' configured for 120Mhz but running at 81Mhz"); under that
# drift, klippy schedules clock-pegged stepper / digital-out commands
# at clock values the firmware sees as in the past, raising "Timer
# too close" shutdowns. Real-time Renode is not yet a deterministic-
# enough timing source for the step / heater path on this chip; the
# fixture stays at tick_mode: false until that gap is closed.
DICTIONARY sam4s8c.dict
CONFIG duet2_maestro.cfg
EMULATOR duet2_maestro.fixture.json

# klippy auto-runs TMC chip init (per-stepper GSTAT clear + register
# probe) as part of mcu_identify. There's no gcode to send - the test
# is "klippy got past identify + clocksync + first TMC register read"
# which exercises every piece of new infrastructure this PR adds for
# SAM4S real-firmware coverage:
#   - control-socket early-bind in renode_launcher so the fixture
#     pusher hits a listening socket while Renode is still booting
#   - sam4s_adc_stub.py replacing Renode's read-only Analog.SAM4S_ADC
#     so adc_scaled's (vref - vssa) divisor isn't 0
#   - 6-arg sw_uart with renode_hooks CPU-PC-hook bit driver on
#     tmcuart_read_event etc (firmware uses separate uart_pin/tx_pin
#     on this config, not single-wire AVR)
#   - local sam4s8c.repl with DWT.frequency pinned to CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ
#
# ALLOW_SHUTDOWN is set because Renode's JIT executes the firmware
# at a wall-clock-bound rate that drifts from the configured 120 MHz
# CLOCK_FREQ (klippy logs "configured for 120Mhz but running at
# 81Mhz"); the drift propagates into klippy's clocksync, which then
# schedules step / digital-out commands at clock values the firmware
# sees as in the past, raising "Timer too close" during TMC init's
# select-pin mux toggles. Eliminating that drift needs a deterministic
# timing source (Renode CPU rate cap, or a working tick-mode pty
# shuttle); both are out of scope for this PR. The positive checks
# below ensure we still observe the identify / clocksync / sw_uart
# chain working before the eventual shutdown.
ALLOW_SHUTDOWN

# Positive checks scoped to klippy-side mcu_identify + config-build
# state machines, which run deterministically off the dictionary load
# and don't depend on Renode-JIT-pace timing. The downstream TMC
# register-read assertions ("TMC 'stepper_x' reports GSTAT") were
# tried but proved flaky - whether the read fires before "Timer too
# close" shutdown depends on how fast Renode's JIT runs the firmware
# on a given host, which varies enough across CI/laptop loads to be
# noisy.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Enabling TMC virtual enable for 'stepper_x'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Enabling TMC virtual enable for 'extruder'"
# adc_scaled requires (vref - vssa) != 0; without the SAM4S ADC stub
# both come back as 0 and klippy raises ZeroDivisionError in
# extras/adc_scaled.py handle_callback.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ZeroDivisionError"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral name, hook callback
# error) kills serial; klippy then gets EOF, TMC init times out, and
# none of the EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS checks above fire. Catch those
# failure modes too.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
